==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is an [[Aku Altar (Enemy Base)|Aku Altar]].
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*3 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*1 [[Possessed Empress]] spawns as the boss after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Capy]] spawns after 36.67 seconds<sup>1,100f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 40~43.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 96.67 seconds<sup>2,900f</sup>.
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 123.33 seconds<sup>3,700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage won't be too bad, just a bit annoying at times.

While not absolutely necessary, a Rich Cat is highly recommended, because the Jackie Pengs have a long respawn delay and the boss appears very quickly into the stage, leaving players with no opportunities to save up. The [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt Cannon|Thunderbolt Cannon]] is recommended, as it can [[Freeze]] anything that doesn't have a Shield, creating an opening when it comes to rushing down Master A.

The first major threat that spawns is Capy, who acts as a single-target nuker that aims to kill your stronger units while Empress wipes meatshields. Powerful attackers like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] must be employed to eat through her 1 million HP as soon as possible before the other threats spawn. At the very least, you want Capy to be on her last knockback by the time Midnite D. arrives.

When Midnite D. does arrive, you want to '''NOT''' lure and kill him, as that will make you lose valuable ground. Instead, mitigate his pushing power with units like [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] or [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]], since Master A. makes lost ground very difficult to get back when he spawns. Killing Midnite D. before that isn't generally feasible nor mandatory, but does help to make the stage far easier.

Master A. is a nuisance as always, constantly chipping at your frontline units while hiding behind Empress at times. Trying to use [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] when Master A. is still alive is out of the question, so you'll usually end up brute forcing the Empress' [[Shield]] here a couple times unless other means of reaching Master A. are available. Do whatever you must to get rid of Master A. '''IMMEDIATELY''', whether that be with [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]], [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]], or any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] that can help with this. Once all three main threats fall, Empress is no longer able to push, and the stage is effectively over.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] - With his [[Explosion]] talent fully upgraded, this fast and powerful rusher is guaranteed to generate one on his first hit that has most of his damage, which gives him an easier time against Master A. whenever if the latter is exposed. In the case of Midnite D. Bahamut can punch right through the Shield, letting the first of the three blasts to cripple him. If supported properly, Bahamut can even straight-up destroy Midnite D. before Master A. emerges, or at the very least damage him sufficiently for other units to finish the job.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] - A fast LD midranger with [[Massive Damage]] to Reds, Courier is one of the few viable non-Uber options to deliver large bursts of damage to Capy, although that's as far as it goes, as its range disadvantage prevents it from contributing meaningfully against Midnite D. and Master A.
*[[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] - Uril, being [[Strong Against]] Aku, can tank a fair bit of damage from them as his level 3 [[Surge Attack]]s gradually whittle them away, while being [[Immune to Surge]] himself. His Curse isn't so useful, but his Slow certainly is when fighting Sinner Snaches, Midnite D. and nasty Condemned Pengs. His cooldown also ensures he could be readily replaced when lost.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Cat Mask Doron]] - A suicide unit with a level 3 Surge Attack, Doron is handy to have for a quick burst of damage, as his extreme health ensures he would not perish before he attacks, and his [[Omni Strike]] (reaches up to 600) will deal great damage
*[[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] - With Move Speed Up and [[Extra Money]], Can Can serves as a powerful, general purpose melee attacker limited by its range and Single Attacks. At level 43+, Can Can does enough damage to instantly kill a Jackie Peng, giving a large burst of income to spam other units. Much like Courier, Can Can is good to have against Capy, but not for everything else.
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]] - A fast and cheap specialist meatshield that is [[Resistant]] to Aku, Maize can easily keep up with the player's faster units and keep the Aku threats stalled, although Research [[Cat Combo]]s may be necessary.

