==Trivia==
*Symphony of Bankruptcy's Japanese name, Dai Go-ban Hatan-chō (第五番破綻調, "No. 5 in Bankruptcy Key"), sounds the same as the Japanese translation of [[wikipedia:Symphony No. 5 (Beethoven)|No. 5 in C Minor]] (第5番 ハ短調) by [[wikipedia:Beethoven|Beethoven]]. The joke is that 破綻調 ("Bankruptcy Key") and ハ短調 ("C minor key") are both pronounced ''hatan-chō''.
**Although 破綻 was officially translated as "Bankruptcy", it can also mean "ruination" or "failure", referencing how [[Possessed Empress]] leads the Cat Empire to utter calamity.
*The [[Sinner Snache]]s in Symphony of Bankruptcy may represent the serpent that tempted Eve in the [[wikipedia:Garden of Eden|Garden of Eden]], as the stage is found in [[Temptation's Rhapsody]] and [[Possessed Empress]]' backstory is somewhat similar to the temptation of Eve.

